From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] frameworks/base: no fixed-orientation letterbox for Droidloom's
 fullscreen tasks

Droidloom's display ignores orientation requests: the host turns it for
the front app instead, as a phone turns for its front activity. Android
letterboxed a fullscreen activity until then, as on a tablet, and apps
such as YouTube gave up their landscape request at once. The activity
now keeps the display's orientation until the host has turned it.

---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
index bd5c72a6..e91204e9 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
@@ -8146,6 +8146,14 @@ final class ActivityRecord extends WindowToken {
             // orientation with insets applied.
             return;
         }
+        // Droidloom: the host turns the display for a fullscreen task's requested
+        // orientation, as a phone does. Letterboxing in the meantime would show the app
+        // its orientation on a display that has not turned, as on a tablet, and apps
+        // such as video players give their request up there.
+        if (mAtmService.mDroidloomTasks != null && task != null
+                && task.getWindowingMode() == WINDOWING_MODE_FULLSCREEN) {
+            return;
+        }
         // TODO(b/232898850): always respect fixed-orientation request.
         // Ignore orientation request for activity in ActivityEmbedding split.
         final TaskFragment organizedTf = getOrganizedTaskFragment();
